          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Razorpay Gets Shareholder Approval for Rs 2,700 Crore IPO as Fintech Bets on AI Amid Rising Losses",
            "articleSection": "Daily Utility",
            "abstract": "Indian fintech giant Razorpay has secured shareholder approval to raise Rs 2,700 crore through an IPO, which will include an offer for sale component and a pre-IPO placement tranche. The company is positioning AI-driven payment infrastructure as a central growth narrative for its public market debut, even as it continues to report net losses amid intense competition in India's digital payments sector. A successful listing would be a major milestone for India's fintech ecosystem and would test public market appetite for loss-making AI-first fintech platforms.",
            "url": "https://www.medianama.com/2026/05/223-exclusive-razorpay-shareholder-approval-rs-2700-crore-ipo/",
            "publisher": {
